#               `PackedFieldExtension::packed_ext_powers` ("Internal error" in
#               `translate_fun_sigs`), and every item bounded by
#               `ExtensionField` reaches it through `ExtensionPacking`.
# Cost:         none in a normal build: every change is behind
#               cfg(hax_backend_lean). In the extracted variant,
#               `PackedFieldExtension::packed_ext_powers` and its 8 impls are
#               absent.
# Upstreamable: no: hiding a required method serves the extractor only; an
#               aeneas fix of the signature is the better fix.
# Drop when:    aeneas translates the signature of `packed_ext_powers`.
# Test:         test p3-baby-bear --test pre_patch_050
# Mutation:     the trait method is gated on the wrong cfg, so a normal build
#               lacks it and its impls no longer compile.
#
# The method returns `Powers<Self>`, a struct over the packed extension type.
#
# aeneas stops on that signature, and so on any item whose bounds name `ExtensionField`.
#
# Under the cfg the trait method and its 8 impls are absent:
#
# - p3-field: the trait, the base field's packing, and the binomial, cubic and quintic packings;
# - p3-binary-field: the tower extensions, Poly192, and its x86-64 packing;
# - p3-mersenne-31: the packed QM31.
#
# Its one caller in the library, `packed_ext_powers_capped`, is already absent there (030).
#
# Seven files import `Powers` only for this method, so their import may go unused under the cfg.
#
# A `cfg_attr` allows that, and is inert in a normal build.
#
# Each attribute shares a line with an existing one, so no line of the extracted source moves.
#
# In a normal build the method is where it was, unchanged, and field-testing's tests run against every impl as shipped.
#
diff --git a/baby-bear/tests/pre_patch_050.rs b/baby-bear/tests/pre_patch_050.rs
